[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104003,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "<p>High-grade B-cell lymphoma with 11q aberration (HGBCL-11q) has the morphology and immunophenotype of Burkitt lymphoma, but it lacks <em>MYC</em> translocations and harbours a characteristic chromosome&nbsp;11q gain/loss pattern. Despite morphological, immunophenotypic, and clinical similarities with Burkitt lymphoma, HGBCL-11q is considered a molecularly distinct tumour type.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-09T17:26:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104004,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "<p>9687/3 High-grade B-cell lymphoma with 11q aberration</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-09T17:26:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104005,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2A85.6 &amp; XH8NN2 Burkitt lymphoma including Burkitt leukaemia &amp; Burkitt-like lymphoma with 11q aberration</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104006,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Acceptable:</em> large B-cell lymphoma with 11q aberration.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> MYC-negative Burkitt lymphoma; Burkitt-like lymphoma with 11q aberration.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-09T17:26:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104007,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104008,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "<p>Most (but not all) cases of HGBCL-11q occur as localized and nodal or extranodal disease {30733272; 32239695}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-09T17:27:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104009,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The clinical features are mass-related. There are no B&nbsp;symptoms {30733272; 32239695}. LBCL-11q may occur in immunocompromised patients {25795716}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104010,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104011,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104012,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "<p>The mutation landscape of these tumours differs from that of Burkitt lymphoma because the ID3/TCF3 pathway,&nbsp;which is one of the biological hallmarks of BL,&nbsp;seems unaffected {30567752; 30733272}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-09T17:27:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104013,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104014,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "<p>Morphologically, HGBCL-11q may be indistinguishable from a typical Burkitt lymphoma; however, it may show more cellular pleomorphism, some variation in nuclear shape, larger nucleoli, or an absence of starry-sky pattern {24398325}. The basic immunophenotype is also similar to that of Burkitt lymphoma: usually it has a mature B-cell phenotype with expression of CD10 and BCL6, a high Ki-67 proliferation index (&ge;&nbsp;90%), and BCL2 is negative (with a few exceptions) {24398325}. There may be variable, sometimes high, expression of MYC protein despite the absence of <em>MYC</em> rearrangement {29327714}.</p>\r\n<p>By immunohistochemistry, HGBCL-11q is LMO2+ and sometimes CD56+ (Burkitt lymphoma is usually negative for these markers); in addition, flow cytometry detection of CD16+/CD56+ in the absence of CD38<sup>higher</sup> or CD8+ are highly characteristic of HGBCL-11q {29327714}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-09T17:28:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104015,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours have vacuolated cytoplasm (known as L3 morphology).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104016,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "<p>The definitive diagnosis of HGBCL-11q relies on the detection of the typical molecular aberration by high-resolution array-based comparative genomic hybridization, with a minimal region of gain in 11q23.3 and a minimal region of loss in 11q24.1-qter {24398325}. A subset of cases show no gain and only the telomeric loss or solely telomeric loss of heterozygosity {24398325}, but rare cases with loss of heterozygosity and no telomeric loss are not detected. Interphase FISH is commonly used as a diagnostic test {29272887; 29327714}. The presence of 11q aberrations is not specific for the disease entity {29272887; 32239695; 26776268}.&nbsp;The mutation landscape of HGBCL-11q is different from that of Burkitt lymphoma: mutations in <em>ID3</em>, <em>TCF3</em>, <em>CCND3</em>, <em>SMARCA4</em>, and <em>MYC</em> are rare, and mutations in <em>GNA13</em> and <em>TTN</em> are frequent {30567752}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-09T17:29:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104017,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a tumour with the morphology and immunophenotype of Burkitt lymphoma; absence of <em>MYC</em> translocations; chromosome&nbsp;11q gain/loss pattern.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104018,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging is performed according to the revised International Pediatric Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma Staging System (IPNHLSS) {25940716}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 104019,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is favourable when treated according to protocols for Burkitt lymphoma {32239695}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-11T16:52:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
